// ======== DEFLATE and zlib, from the deflate package ========
//
// The DEFLATE reader and writer, zlib framing and the checksums that PNG
// stands on live in the 'deflate' package. This package imports it (see the
// root) and keeps the spellings it always had:
//
//   inflate, zlibDecompress, zlibCompress, adler32, Crc32   as deflate's own
//   deflate(data, level)    deflate's 'rawDeflate' (the name 'deflate' is
//                           the package's own, so the function could not be
//                           called that there)
//
// The error of 'inflate' and 'zlibDecompress' is deflate's DeflateError; its
// 'reason' and 'message()' are what a DecodeError's are.

// Compress to a raw DEFLATE stream at 'level' (0 stored, 1 fixed Huffman,
// 2 dynamic Huffman; other values are 2)
pub fn deflate(data &Array[u8], level i32) List[u8] {
  flate.rawDeflate(data, level);
}
